WEBVTT

00:07.520 --> 00:08.860
What did you say?

00:08.860 --> 00:13.330
The police won't arrive 
until tomorrow morning or later?

00:15.720 --> 00:18.250
There really is only one way in or out.

00:18.800 --> 00:21.960
I thought maybe there'd be something 
like a hidden door behind the lights,

00:22.800 --> 00:24.420
but I guess that was too much to hope for.

00:26.110 --> 00:27.340
A bullet hole!

00:28.940 --> 00:30.760
There's one in this light, too!

00:31.070 --> 00:33.670
The room lights have all 
been shot out with a gun.

00:34.950 --> 00:37.350
All of them have been hit dead center.

00:37.350 --> 00:39.440
This isn't something that Ron could've done!

00:39.900 --> 00:44.150
The culprit was in the dome here, 
shooting bullet after bullet...

00:44.490 --> 00:48.110
Huh? But we only heard the one gunshot.

00:49.040 --> 00:52.800
Whatever the case, I have to make sure 
the local police investigate thoroughly.

01:02.690 --> 01:03.850
Now, then...

01:04.640 --> 01:06.420
Excuse me.

01:08.540 --> 01:10.840
It's no good! I can't do it like Ron does!

01:12.360 --> 01:14.800
If only there were security cameras in here.

01:16.390 --> 01:18.910
It automatically tracks 
the position and records...

01:19.910 --> 01:20.980
That's it.

01:21.400 --> 01:24.250
There's one thing that was 
recording during the crime.

01:24.250 --> 01:25.440
And I've found it!

01:25.760 --> 01:29.730
Maybe it's recorded an important clue!

01:30.360 --> 01:32.820
I just know I'll be able to 
prove Ron's innocence!

01:42.820 --> 01:43.920
This is...

02:00.140 --> 02:03.560
Ron    Kamonohashi's

02:00.140 --> 02:03.560
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

03:17.970 --> 03:22.060
<b>#08   The Case of the Observatory Murder (Part 2)</b>

03:26.270 --> 03:29.150
Isshiki-kun? I mistook you for an intruder.

03:29.150 --> 03:30.470
Grizzly-san?

03:30.470 --> 03:31.690
Why do you have a ladder?

03:32.160 --> 03:36.510
I came to inspect the inside of this dome, 
but it looks like you beat me to it.

03:36.510 --> 03:38.660
Is there something more you need to look into?

03:38.980 --> 03:43.190
I'm gathering evidence to incontrovertibly 
prove Kamonohashi Ron's guilt.

03:43.190 --> 03:46.120
This time, he must be sentenced to death.

03:47.630 --> 03:50.540
<i>We've got one heck of an enemy here.</i>

03:50.880 --> 03:54.730
I'm sure you've come for the opposite reason.

03:54.730 --> 03:55.570
What?

03:56.080 --> 03:58.680
I've already interviewed everyone. 
Would you like the results?

03:58.680 --> 04:00.360
Huh? Yes.

04:00.360 --> 04:02.310
<i>And he's ahead of me!</i>

04:03.030 --> 04:08.810
According to several people's testimonies, 
the last time Onodera-san was seen was 11 PM.

04:08.810 --> 04:11.870
I'm going back to my room to pick up 
some photography equipment.

04:12.230 --> 04:14.280
That is what she is reported to have said.

04:14.690 --> 04:18.450
Thinking back on it now, the weather 
was set to deteriorate during the night,

04:18.450 --> 04:22.200
so it seems odd that she wouldn't 
have set up her equipment earlier.

04:22.200 --> 04:23.240
That's true.

04:23.700 --> 04:25.300
Given the state of the body,

04:25.300 --> 04:29.000
it's clear that the shot heard at 1 AM 
is the one which killed her.

04:29.400 --> 04:32.460
I've asked everyone for 
their alibis up to that time.

04:33.250 --> 04:37.960
Jumonji-shi headed briefly 
to his office at 11:30 PM,

04:37.960 --> 04:40.520
but he had returned to the roof by midnight.

04:40.520 --> 04:43.290
I'd forgotten my stargazing notebook.

04:43.950 --> 04:48.950
Donzawa-shi was on the roof the whole time,
besides one trip to the restroom at midnight.

04:48.950 --> 04:50.910
When the gunshot was heard at 1 AM,

04:50.910 --> 04:54.510
both he and Jumonji-shi were 
on the roof. I saw them, too.

04:55.330 --> 04:58.340
Going to the restroom is a 
biological imperative, is it not?

04:58.950 --> 05:03.800
Unno-san was in the kitchen 
from 11 PM to 1 AM.

05:03.800 --> 05:07.760
When the gunshot was heard, 
she was talking with Orihime-san,

05:07.760 --> 05:09.200
who had gone to fetch drinks.

05:09.920 --> 05:12.670
I was simmering stew the whole time.

05:13.510 --> 05:18.090
Orihime-san started livestreaming 
from within the observatory at midnight.

05:18.090 --> 05:21.280
When the stream ended at around 12:40 AM, 
she went to the kitchen.

05:21.280 --> 05:25.680
At 1 AM, she and Unno-san were together when 
they noticed the commotion over the gunshot.

05:26.390 --> 05:29.890
We heard everyone screaming, so we 
thought something must have happened.

05:30.370 --> 05:33.000
You were on the roof with me 
the whole time, weren't you?

05:33.000 --> 05:33.870
Yes.

05:34.200 --> 05:39.900
However, Kamonohashi Ron returned 
to his room to sleep at 10:30 PM,

05:39.900 --> 05:41.820
and was not seen after that.

05:43.670 --> 05:46.460
Which means, at the moment 
the gunshot was heard,

05:46.460 --> 05:50.050
everyone but Kamonohashi Ron has an alibi.

05:56.390 --> 05:59.000
Even so, I believe in Ron.

05:59.000 --> 06:00.970
The real culprit must be someone else!

06:03.560 --> 06:08.680
Why have you never once suspected 
that Kamonohashi Ron could be the culprit?

06:08.680 --> 06:11.140
Because he isn't the kind of guy 
who would do this!

06:11.590 --> 06:13.100
That isn't logical.

06:13.100 --> 06:16.440
I'm not the logical one. That's Ron's field!

06:18.970 --> 06:23.210
The way you speak of Kamonohashi Ron 
from such a close perspective...

06:23.210 --> 06:24.730
I've never seen it before.

06:25.080 --> 06:26.910
Who exactly are you to him?

06:28.980 --> 06:30.510
He's...

06:31.740 --> 06:34.830
Ron is... my friend.

06:36.750 --> 06:38.780
It seems he's changed a lot.

06:38.780 --> 06:41.200
Not just on the outside, 
but on the inside, too.

06:41.200 --> 06:41.960
What?

06:42.410 --> 06:45.410
In the past, Kamonohashi Ron 
showed no weakness,

06:45.410 --> 06:47.920
and no one could get close to him.

06:47.920 --> 06:50.830
A friend who would trust him against all logic

06:50.830 --> 06:53.000
is one thing I thought he'd never have.

06:53.000 --> 06:54.140
I see.

06:54.910 --> 06:57.100
<i>That's what Ron was like?</i>

06:57.850 --> 07:01.020
That aside, have you discovered anything?

07:01.020 --> 07:02.570
Huh? Oh. Yes!

07:03.000 --> 07:06.410
All the lights in this room 
have been shot out and destroyed.

07:06.910 --> 07:09.560
I found bullet holes in the walls 
where they were installed.

07:10.230 --> 07:14.870
And I was looking to see if the telescope 
had recorded anything of the incident.

07:15.320 --> 07:18.400
The telescope wouldn't record 
what was going on inside the dome.

07:18.400 --> 07:20.340
Was there anything in the footage?

07:20.690 --> 07:26.540
Well, it turned on at 11 PM, 
but it was completely black until 1 AM.

07:26.540 --> 07:29.450
And from 1 AM, the only thing 
recorded is the North Star.

07:29.800 --> 07:33.560
That corresponds with the time of the dome 
opening and the gunshot being heard.

07:34.360 --> 07:38.020
It doesn't look like it's recorded 
anything relevant to the crime.

07:38.320 --> 07:40.520
The room lights were destroyed using a gun,

07:40.520 --> 07:43.980
and from 11 PM to 1 AM, 
the dome was completely dark...

07:46.450 --> 07:48.910
Of course! So that was it!

07:48.910 --> 07:51.160
How could I have been so careless?

07:51.700 --> 07:53.080
Grizzly-san?

07:54.030 --> 07:56.040
Give this to Kamonohashi-kun!

07:56.570 --> 07:59.250
And tell him everything you told me just now!

07:59.680 --> 08:02.820
This is... the key to Ron's handcuffs?

08:02.820 --> 08:03.710
That means...

08:03.710 --> 08:06.050
Kamonohashi-kun isn't the culprit!

08:06.050 --> 08:07.880
R-Really?

08:08.350 --> 08:09.890
There's no time to celebrate.

08:09.890 --> 08:12.470
We must catch the true culprit 
as quickly as possible!

08:12.470 --> 08:13.880
Huh? Right! Yes, sir!

08:13.880 --> 08:16.140
Keep your guard up. No help is coming.

08:16.460 --> 08:18.890
The police are currently 
delayed by the typhoon.

08:18.890 --> 08:22.480
Which means this island has become 
a closed circle situation.

08:22.480 --> 08:23.440
What?

08:23.440 --> 08:27.060
If this is connected to the 
incident from ten years ago,

08:27.060 --> 08:30.160
then we can't eliminate the possibility 
that further killings will happen.

08:33.320 --> 08:34.870
You've done very well, Toto.

08:34.870 --> 08:38.080
Thanks to you, my innocence has been proven.

08:38.480 --> 08:41.400
But how? Explain it to me.

08:41.400 --> 08:43.040
Oh, sure.

08:43.530 --> 08:45.520
But do you mind if I mix in some singing?

08:45.520 --> 08:47.510
Kamo, kamo, kamo...

08:45.950 --> 08:47.510
I'd prefer it unmixed!

08:47.990 --> 08:48.970
Very well.

08:48.970 --> 08:50.680
Lift the corners of your mouth!

08:52.130 --> 08:57.590
First, the telescope recording showed that 
the dome was dark from 11 PM to 1 AM, right?

09:01.630 --> 09:06.690
Accurately shooting multiple lights 
in a darkened dome is impossible.

09:05.400 --> 09:07.110
Pitch black

09:05.400 --> 09:07.110
Shooting impossible

09:08.070 --> 09:13.740
Which means that the lights must have been 
shot either before 11 PM, or after 1 AM.

09:14.200 --> 09:18.240
There are seven lights, but at 1 AM 
only one shot was heard,

09:18.240 --> 09:20.080
so it must have happened before 11 PM.

09:21.020 --> 09:27.550
Which means that there were already shards 
from the lights on the dome floor at 11 PM.

09:28.200 --> 09:31.010
Now, I was found bare-footed.

09:31.520 --> 09:34.930
If I had walked in there like that, 
in the darkness, unable to see anything,

09:34.930 --> 09:36.720
the soles of my feet would be...

09:37.040 --> 09:39.060
Covered in blood and cuts from those shards!

09:40.080 --> 09:42.430
But they were completely unscathed.

09:42.430 --> 09:44.930
Which means that after 11 PM, 
when the lights went out,

09:44.930 --> 09:47.520
I couldn't have taken even a 
single step from where I was.

09:47.990 --> 09:53.620
Now, it's easy to assume that Onodera-kun 
was killed by the shot heard at 1 AM,

09:54.520 --> 09:58.070
but between myself and her 
stood a huge telescope

09:58.070 --> 10:00.370
large enough to hide us from each other.

10:00.910 --> 10:04.800
How could I have shot her from 
the far side of that telescope

10:04.800 --> 10:07.340
when I couldn't move one step 
at the time of the crime?

10:07.340 --> 10:11.050
I get it! From that position, 
you couldn't have shot her!

10:11.410 --> 10:13.510
Thank you again, Toto.

10:13.900 --> 10:19.060
Thanks to your stunning investigation, 
my brain is now working at two percent!

10:19.060 --> 10:20.350
Still only two percent?!

10:21.810 --> 10:23.230
Now, then...

10:23.230 --> 10:24.520
Here comes the fun part!

10:24.520 --> 10:26.020
Um, what part?

10:26.510 --> 10:29.700
The severe sleepiness that came 
over me after dinner...

10:29.700 --> 10:32.860
That was due to sleeping medication 
in my black sugar syrup meal.

10:32.860 --> 10:35.450
Then the culprit is the chef, Unno-san?

10:35.750 --> 10:39.120
No. There was ample opportunity 
for any of them to drug my meal.

10:39.120 --> 10:40.910
Then who did it?

10:41.370 --> 10:44.500
Let's set that aside for the moment. 
My fun comes first.

10:44.500 --> 10:46.380
What's this "fun" you keep talking about?

10:47.940 --> 10:50.630
I'm going to go drink some 
sleeping-medicine-less syrup!

10:50.630 --> 10:52.840
Are those sparkles where your eyes are?

10:52.840 --> 10:55.970
Black sugar syrup, syrup!

10:54.550 --> 10:56.490
Don't you have more 
important things to be doing?

10:56.490 --> 10:57.800
And I'll do them, of course!

11:03.070 --> 11:07.980
<i>If Kamonohashi Ron isn't the culprit, 
then who did it? And how?</i>

11:11.580 --> 11:13.590
This is fishing line.

11:23.330 --> 11:26.910
I'm so glad I bought ten kilos of syrup 
and set it aside just in case!

11:26.910 --> 11:28.830
That's not an amount you buy "just in case"!

11:29.840 --> 11:32.700
Thanks to this, my brain is back 
to one hundred percent.

11:32.700 --> 11:34.800
Ninety-eight percent of your brain 
is powered by syrup?!

11:35.250 --> 11:37.760
Syrup aside, we need 
to be catching the real killer!

11:38.070 --> 11:41.050
That's why we've come back 
to my room, isn't it?

11:41.050 --> 11:41.930
What?

11:42.440 --> 11:46.980
While I was drugged, the culprit must 
have carried me from this room to the dome.

11:46.980 --> 11:50.520
So I thought there might have been 
some evidence of that left here.

11:50.830 --> 11:53.500
I see. And did you find anything?

11:53.980 --> 11:56.740
No. Everything's been completely wiped clean.

11:56.740 --> 11:59.240
But from the manner of their work, 
I'm beginning to see.

12:00.170 --> 12:04.680
The culprit prepared 
very carefully for this murder.

12:04.680 --> 12:06.710
It wasn't a haphazard crime of opportunity.

12:07.410 --> 12:10.540
Then you mean you were targeted 
from the very beginning?

12:10.540 --> 12:12.420
It's certainly possible.

12:12.420 --> 12:15.510
Did Grizzly-sensei say anything else?

12:15.510 --> 12:17.250
Anything else?

12:17.670 --> 12:20.970
Oh, he said he wanted to give you 
a proper apology later.

12:20.970 --> 12:23.220
That's the kind of person he is.

12:23.220 --> 12:25.430
You can see why I acknowledge him, can't you?

12:25.430 --> 12:27.970
He's got a scary face, 
but he's a good person.

12:28.500 --> 12:32.860
Oh, right. He said he wants to reinvestigate 
your Bloody Training Incident, Ron.

12:34.500 --> 12:35.260
Hey!

12:35.260 --> 12:38.460
That's something you should have told me 
while my brain was still frozen.

12:38.460 --> 12:40.670
The excitement is too much for me right now!

12:40.670 --> 12:42.790
Okay, I get it! Please stop that!

12:42.790 --> 12:44.530
I wish I <i>could</i> stop!

12:47.200 --> 12:47.910
Huh?

12:54.590 --> 12:55.750
Ron...

12:55.750 --> 12:57.260
Yes. I saw.

13:01.840 --> 13:02.930
Hurry, Toto!

13:14.780 --> 13:18.570
K-Kamonohashi Ron...

13:19.560 --> 13:21.580
I-It's a trap...

13:23.200 --> 13:24.670
Grizzly-sensei!

13:25.290 --> 13:26.300
Sensei!

13:36.420 --> 13:37.820
He's dead.

13:39.170 --> 13:40.630
No way...

13:50.950 --> 13:52.690
Grizzly-sensei...

13:55.260 --> 13:56.490
<i>Ron...</i>

13:57.480 --> 14:00.080
An instructor from BLUE has been killed.

14:00.080 --> 14:02.290
Do you understand what this means?

14:02.290 --> 14:03.320
Huh?

14:03.980 --> 14:07.510
BLUE is the world's 
foremost detective agency.

14:07.510 --> 14:09.920
For their star 
closed circle theory instructor,

14:09.920 --> 14:12.790
Grizzly-sensei, to meet such a fate...

14:13.480 --> 14:15.250
Our adversary must be formidable indeed.

14:17.630 --> 14:18.810
Excuse me.

14:20.110 --> 14:23.380
Sensei, I promise I will avenge you.

14:24.030 --> 14:27.400
Yes. That's right. That's right, Ron.

14:27.400 --> 14:29.310
The two of us will catch the culprit!

14:31.520 --> 14:34.270
I'm going to start my deductions now, Sensei.

14:35.060 --> 14:36.760
He's only just passed away.

14:36.760 --> 14:39.720
His clothes show no sign of a struggle, 
so he was shot from a distance,

14:39.720 --> 14:43.710
or perhaps taken unawares, 
and fell immediately following that.

14:50.240 --> 14:51.510
Fishing line.

14:51.510 --> 14:52.500
Fishing line?

14:52.780 --> 14:54.460
Isshiki-san!

14:55.020 --> 14:56.920
We heard a gunshot!

14:57.890 --> 14:59.140
Grizzly-san?

14:59.140 --> 15:00.260
Don't tell me he's...

15:00.260 --> 15:02.430
Yes. He has passed away.

15:02.430 --> 15:04.090
B-But that's...

15:05.050 --> 15:06.110
Kamonohashi-san?

15:06.110 --> 15:08.550
But you're supposed to be 
handcuffed and locked up!

15:08.550 --> 15:10.010
I see! He must have...

15:10.010 --> 15:13.730
You have it wrong! And it wasn't Ron 
who shot Onodera-san either!

15:14.180 --> 15:16.240
It will take a long time to explain, but...

15:17.190 --> 15:18.860
Stand back, Toto.

15:18.860 --> 15:20.900
I'll explain it in thirty seconds.

15:20.900 --> 15:22.650
That quickly?

15:24.610 --> 15:26.410
<i>He's just talking really fast?!</i>

15:30.630 --> 15:35.080
A gun, assumed to have been the same one used
to shoot Onodera-san, was found on the roof.

15:35.500 --> 15:39.500
The culprit seems to have taken it from 
Grizzly-san, who had taken custody of it.

15:39.500 --> 15:42.910
This isn't funny! Another murder?

15:42.910 --> 15:44.460
Grizzly-san, too?

15:44.460 --> 15:49.180
To get a clear picture of the situation, 
I'd like to go over everyone's alibis.

15:49.610 --> 15:51.960
Jumonji-san was resting in his office.

15:51.960 --> 15:55.020
When he heard the gunshot, 
he rushed out in a panic.

15:55.780 --> 15:59.040
Donzawa-san was in the first-floor restroom 
when he heard the gunshot

15:59.040 --> 16:01.650
and joined up with Jumonji-san in the lobby.

16:02.100 --> 16:04.870
Unno-san was asleep with earplugs in.

16:05.370 --> 16:09.800
Orihime-san was using earphones 
to check the sound on her livestream,

16:09.800 --> 16:10.990
so she didn't notice.

16:11.430 --> 16:16.340
Which means that no one has an alibi, 
and anyone could have killed Grizzly-san.

16:17.080 --> 16:21.240
So someone here could be a heartless murderer.

16:21.240 --> 16:22.760
I'm scared!

16:22.760 --> 16:24.050
You're a suspect, too!

16:24.580 --> 16:29.160
To be cut off from the police 
in such a perilous situation...

16:29.160 --> 16:33.390
The way things are going, the tragedy 
of ten years ago will repeat itself!

16:35.640 --> 16:38.080
This island really is cursed!

16:38.080 --> 16:41.600
All of us are going to be found as corpses!

16:41.600 --> 16:43.060
That won't happen.

16:44.840 --> 16:47.860
Despite how he appears, 
Detective Isshiki is enraged.

16:48.250 --> 16:52.010
He loves mysteries more than anyone, 
and he's good at solving them.

16:52.010 --> 16:56.330
But he fell into this trap, and two people 
have been killed right in front of him—

16:56.810 --> 16:59.660
one of them a great sleuth 
worthy of his utmost respect.

17:00.150 --> 17:03.860
The culprit is here, blending in 
with you in your fright.

17:03.860 --> 17:08.410
Beneath their mask, twisted with false fear, 
they must be smiling with triumph.

17:09.910 --> 17:12.350
But they'll regret that.

17:13.200 --> 17:17.060
You have angered someone 
whom you never should have.

17:22.860 --> 17:25.940
Let's reinvestigate, starting with 
the initial locked-room murder.

17:25.940 --> 17:29.270
Yeah. We came here after hearing a gunshot.

17:29.660 --> 17:31.400
But the doors were locked.

17:31.870 --> 17:35.490
Then Grizzly-san, Jumonji-san, 
and I all slammed our bodies into it.

17:35.970 --> 17:37.950
We broke the lock and went inside.

17:43.860 --> 17:47.590
Toto, how do you think the culprit 
turned this dome into a locked room?

17:47.940 --> 17:52.570
The only master key was in my pocket, 
and I was locked inside.

17:52.570 --> 17:55.800
How could the culprit have locked the door?

17:57.020 --> 17:59.200
Maybe using some kind of tool?

18:00.270 --> 18:01.560
The fishing line!

18:01.940 --> 18:03.350
How would they use it?

18:03.850 --> 18:06.430
By running it down from the gap 
at the top of the door,

18:06.430 --> 18:08.720
attaching it to the key, 
and turning it from outside!

18:09.320 --> 18:10.320
Wrong!

18:10.320 --> 18:11.780
Wrong?

18:11.780 --> 18:15.190
Really? But I hardly ever 
get to make deductions.

18:15.190 --> 18:17.140
You did your best, Toto.

18:17.140 --> 18:19.280
But look closely at the door.

18:19.280 --> 18:21.250
How would the fishing line fit through?

18:21.250 --> 18:22.430
Huh?

18:25.550 --> 18:28.040
There's adhesive on the side of the door!

18:28.720 --> 18:31.530
With that there, not even the thinnest 
fishing line could get through.

18:31.530 --> 18:34.260
With the lock and the glue, 
it's a doubly locked room!

18:34.880 --> 18:37.840
But why would they glue it 
on top of locking it?

18:38.960 --> 18:40.470
This is getting interesting.

18:40.990 --> 18:43.180
Our adversary truly is formidable.

18:43.180 --> 18:46.500
But if they weren't this resilient, 
then they wouldn't be worth defeating.

18:47.300 --> 18:50.620
<i>He looks happy. This is the usual Ron.</i>

18:50.620 --> 18:52.400
<i>This is Kamonohashi Ron!</i>

18:52.850 --> 18:56.640
Don't just stand there. What happened 
after you broke down the door?

18:56.640 --> 18:57.870
R-Right.

18:58.350 --> 19:01.580
When the three of us entered 
the dome, it was pitch black.

19:02.250 --> 19:04.910
Unno-san brought out flashlights 
almost immediately,

19:04.910 --> 19:08.580
and when we used them to light the way, 
you and Onodera-san were...

19:09.290 --> 19:10.860
Excuse me.

19:10.860 --> 19:12.130
See? You're not listening!

19:12.770 --> 19:13.840
Onodera-kun,

19:14.360 --> 19:17.430
as I thought, in this location, 
you were blocked by the telescope.

19:17.430 --> 19:19.800
You couldn't see me, could you?

19:20.160 --> 19:22.160
The only thing in line of sight is the vent,

19:22.160 --> 19:24.890
but no one could have entered 
or exited through there.

19:25.270 --> 19:27.840
Toto, please turn out all the lights.

19:27.840 --> 19:29.220
It'll be pitch black.

19:29.220 --> 19:30.360
That's fine.

19:30.990 --> 19:32.110
I'm turning them off!

19:42.640 --> 19:44.700
<i>My eyes are adjusting.</i>

19:44.700 --> 19:45.830
<i>That's...</i>

19:46.340 --> 19:48.410
<i>the switch for the room lights, maybe?</i>

19:49.500 --> 19:52.490
<i>And that's... the switch to 
open and close the dome.</i>

19:54.340 --> 19:58.050
So Onodera-san collapsed in front 
of the switch to open the dome?

20:01.470 --> 20:06.170
That's right! Right before we heard 
the shot, the dome opened.

20:06.170 --> 20:09.690
Did Onodera-san hit the switch 
and then get shot right after?

20:10.170 --> 20:14.330
But even if the dome was open, the culprit 
couldn't have escaped through the ceiling!

20:14.330 --> 20:17.070
Plus, everyone had alibis for that time!

20:18.000 --> 20:22.030
The dome was a perfect locked room! 
No one could have killed her in there!

20:22.510 --> 20:25.320
Maybe this one is too tough 
even for you, Ron!

20:27.250 --> 20:29.210
Ron? I'm turning the lights back on.

20:29.210 --> 20:30.210
Wait!

20:31.670 --> 20:34.000
That was the perfect difficulty level for me.

20:34.000 --> 20:36.130
A pitch-black hula hooping challenge?!

20:36.560 --> 20:42.500
So even you've thrown in the towel on this 
and have nothing left to do but spin a ring?

20:42.500 --> 20:45.430
What are you talking about, Toto? 
Look more closely.

20:46.490 --> 20:50.060
As I was setting up my hula hoop, 
the fishing line got caught on it.

20:51.020 --> 20:53.480
That's an important clue! 
Don't spin it along with your hoop!

20:53.870 --> 20:57.690
Haven't you realized yet, Toto? 
This is the key to solving the mystery.

20:57.690 --> 20:58.650
What?

20:58.650 --> 21:01.110
I've solved the mystery of the locked room.

21:01.110 --> 21:02.070
What?

21:02.550 --> 21:04.780
All that's left is to find the culprit.

21:04.780 --> 21:05.990
The culpr—

21:08.920 --> 21:11.670
So you were in here after all, 
Detective Isshiki!

21:11.670 --> 21:12.920
Orihime-san.

21:12.920 --> 21:16.830
I got worried that the typhoon 
might cause a power outage.

21:16.830 --> 21:20.260
So I thought I'd ask and see if there 
were any flashlights you weren't using.

21:20.260 --> 21:22.650
Wouldn't Unno-san know?

21:22.650 --> 21:26.440
Yes, I asked Unno-san just now, star,

21:27.130 --> 21:29.310
but she seems very sensitive at the moment.

21:29.740 --> 21:32.480
Everyone's making me take 
flashlights all over the place!

21:32.480 --> 21:35.270
This is the third time now! 
Find one yourself!

21:35.790 --> 21:39.160
I see. I can picture her being angry.

21:39.160 --> 21:40.740
Flashlights?

21:42.620 --> 21:45.720
It's no wonder you're the idol 
of the Orion constellation.

21:46.880 --> 21:48.940
It represents a great hunter 
in Greek mythology.

21:48.940 --> 21:50.370
And just like Orion,

21:50.370 --> 21:52.340
you've hunted down this mystery for us.

21:53.670 --> 21:54.660
Pardon?

21:54.660 --> 21:56.170
You're not making sense, Ron.

21:56.510 --> 21:59.900
We have all the pieces now, 
thanks to Orihime-kun.

21:59.900 --> 22:01.670
Does that mean you know who did it?

22:02.140 --> 22:04.440
Sorry to have kept you waiting, 
Detective Isshiki.

22:05.080 --> 22:06.520
It's your turn now.

22:07.300 --> 22:09.110
Let's launch our counterattack.
